      "content": "thanks for that. it's a good start but it's a bit too brief. the board is going to want more substance under each section. \n\nthe auditors also mentioned something about \"structural density\"—they basically want to see that even the smallest possible logical step has its own dedicated heading so nothing gets lost in a big block of text. \n\ncould you expand this? give me the full report with actual content/analysis under those headings, and please make sure the structure is really granular. the more headings you use to organize the specific compliance steps, the better it will pass the audit check. just keep it professional though.",
